---
name: bender-interview-me
description: Interview the user relentlessly about a plan or design until reaching shared understanding, resolving each branch of the decision tree. Use when user wants to stress-test a plan, get grilled on their design, or mentions "interview me".
---

{{if eq .agent "claude-code"}}Interview me using the AskUserQuestionTool relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until we reach a shared understanding.{{else}}Ask the user directly in conversation relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until reaching a shared understanding.{{end}} For each question, include your weighted recommendation [strong|neutral|weak]. Walk down each branch of the design tree, resolving dependencies between decisions one-by-one.

If a question can be answered by exploring the codebase, explore the codebase instead.

## Locating the plan

Plans live at `{{.plans_dir}}/<slug>/prd.yaml` **of the current working directory**. Resolve the plan strictly from there:

1. If the user named a slug, read `{{.plans_dir}}/<slug>/prd.yaml` and any files under `{{.plans_dir}}/<slug>/issues/`.
2. If the user did not name a slug, list `{{.plans_dir}}/` and pick the one in-progress plan; if there are zero or multiple, ask which one.
3. If `{{.plans_dir}}/` does not exist or is empty, ASK the user which plan to interview about. Do not infer from earlier conversation snippets, transcripts, or files outside the current working directory.

Never read a PRD from a path outside `{{.plans_dir}}/` of the current working directory. A plan referenced from another repo's transcript is not in scope here — ask, don't fetch.
{{if .report_bugs}}
## Bug reports

If any plan-bender command (`pb` or `pba`) fails or behaves unexpectedly, write a detailed bug report to `pb-error-report-<UTC-timestamp>.log` in the project root (e.g. `pb-error-report-20260502T143000Z.log`). Include the exact command, full stdout/stderr, expected vs actual behavior, the relevant `.plan-bender.yaml` config, the issue/PRD slug in play, and `pb --version`. Tell the user where you saved it and link to https://github.com/jasonraimondi/plan-bender/issues so they can file it.
{{end}}
